<title>AUSTRIA: ALPINE SKIING-TOMBA WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-TOMBA WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>SCHLADMING, Austria 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Alberto Tomba won a men's Alpine skiing World Cup slalom on Thursday in a combined time of one minute 35.87 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Austria's Thomas Stangassinger finished second in 1:36.03</p>
<p>and Sebastien Amiez of France was third in 1:36.19, also</p>
<p>according to provisional results.</p>
</text>
